    "description": "## Outcome and context\n\nDecision made on WAGR-407 — flag fraud directly in the Sign-Ups related list on Player instead of building a separate Fraud Flags related list. This ticket implements that decision.\n\n## Current state\n\n* The Sign-Ups related list already exists on the Player page (WAGR-197).\n* `Fraud_Flag__c` and `Fraud_Review_Status__c` already exist on Sign_Up__c — confirmed via a live sandbox schema check (Sep 16, 2026).\n* Neither field is currently surfaced as a column on the Sign-Ups related list.\n\n## Proposed solution\n\n1. Add `Fraud_Flag__c` (Fraud) and `Fraud_Review_Status__c` (Fraud Review Status) as columns to the Sign-Ups related list's column set on the Player page layout / Lightning page.\n2. No new fields, objects, or automation required — this is a column-set change only.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. Fraud and Fraud Review Status both appear as columns on the Sign-Ups related list on the Player record page.\n2. No other columns, ordering, or configuration on the related list is disturbed.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n* The underlying fraud business rule / automation (what sets these fields, when) — tracked separately under WAGR-295 and WAGR-1, still open.\n* Any change to the Sign_Up__c fields themselves — they already exist as-is.\n\n## Source\n\n* WAGR-407 — decision ticket this implements\n* Emily Vandenberg, doc comment (Sep 14, 2026) — asked to simplify and flag fraud directly in the Sign-Up list\n* Sandbox schema check (Sep 16, 2026) confirming both fields already exist on Sign_Up__c\n\n",
